\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Run It Twice: an 8-hour, single-page version\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 I read all 45 pages of the proposal and looked at the live colossal.com. The asset list in your prompt still said 
\f2\fs26 \{\{AVAILABLE_ASSETS\}\}
\f1\fs24 , so I've treated the PDF as the only thing supplied. Every product and market fact below comes from the proposal. Where I've simplified something or had to assume something, I say so.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 \strokec2 A. The simplified idea\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Run It Twice
\f1\b0  is one scrolling page with eight full-screen sections. Seven are static pages of large type. One is a working simulation, and it is the only part of the page that moves.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f3\i \cf0 This experience takes the audience from "Chain is our AI assistant" to "Chain is the control layer, and only we can show it today" by showing one procedure run, stop for a human decision, and run again with a matching record.
\f1\i0 \
The story: banks are moving to ledgers that run 24/7 while their controls keep office hours. Every vendor uses the same three words. The regulators have left a blank page on agentic AI. One claim is still open to us: same inputs, same outputs, every run recorded. Watch it happen, keep the record, then make three decisions.\
The proposal's own reasoning was that repeatability can't be claimed, only watched. This version keeps that one mechanism (the second run matching the first) and cuts the presenter tooling around it.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

